   "body": "**Adversarial review (Opus 5.5, independent of the author): REQUEST CHANGES** — head 81bf54e00cad7b09cf26402766fc7af6c024aae3\n\n1. **High**, `ReplyComposerModel+ArchivedDrafts.swift:36,62,81,93`: the app does not compile. `draftWarning` is `private(set)` (`ReplyComposerModel.swift:53`), and this extension in another file assigns it four times (`cannot assign to property: setter is inaccessible`). Fix: move the methods into `ReplyComposerModel.swift`, or add an internal setter helper; then run the App tests on CI/Mac.\n2. **Medium**, `discardArchived` / `discardAllArchived` do not check `isMovingDrafts` or `canEdit` (LESSONS 11). Scenario: tap a row whose text differs from the editor's, `use()` archives X and suspends; \"Vider\" runs between the two `archiveReply` calls; the second call restores only the picked draft, so X is lost. Fix: both return early while `isMovingDrafts`, and the sheet's buttons are disabled meanwhile.\n3. **Low**, `ArchivedDraftsFormat.swift:34`: `.shortened` shows \"2:05 PM\" in en_US; legacy uses the fixed `\"HH:mm\"` (`AnswerView.swift:1989` @ 87fe0d1c). Fix: fixed 24-hour format.\n4. **Low**: no test covers the pending-autosave / `isMovingDrafts` claim of the spec.\n5. **Nit**: make `archivedDrafts`, `draftSource`, `pickedArchivedID`, `isMovingDrafts` `private(set)` once the extension is in the same file; `ArchivedDraftsView.swift:66` says \"par sujet\", legacy \"par topic\".\n\n**Checked**: 36 engine tests green; three mutations each failed a test; Codable of older files still decodes; no other exhaustive `switch` over `DraftContext`; no ledger file touched; Closes/Claim lines; no draft text logged; lines ≤ 140; legacy citations; every LESSONS row.\n\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
